      "summaries": {
        "en": "Claude Cookbooks is a collection of Jupyter notebooks demonstrating practical applications of Anthropic's Claude AI model, helping developers understand how to effectively leverage large language models for real-world tasks. The project stands out by providing hands-on, executable examples that reveal Claude's capabilities through concrete implementations rather than abstract descriptions. Developers can use these recipes as starting points for their own projects—from building conversational agents to automating document analysis—by modifying the provided code to experiment with different prompts and workflows.",
        "zh": "Claude Cookbooks 是一个基于 Jupyter Notebook 的实用教程集合，展示了如何将 Anthropic 的 Claude 大语言模型应用于实际开发场景。该项目通过可执行的代码示例而非理论描述，让开发者直观理解如何通过提示工程和任务分解来发挥 Claude 的推理与生成能力。这些“食谱”覆盖了从对话系统构建到文档处理等多种用例，开发者可直接运行并修改其中的代码，将其作为自己项目的起点，探索如何将大模型集成到工作流中解决具体问题。",
        "es": "Claude Cookbooks is a collection of Jupyter notebooks demonstrating practical applications of Anthropic's Claude AI model, helping developers understand how to effectively leverage large language models for real-world tasks. The project stands out by providing hands-on, executable examples that reveal Claude's capabilities through concrete implementations rather than abstract descriptions. Developers can use these recipes as starting points for their own projects—from building conversational agents to automating document analysis—by modifying the provided code to experiment with different prompts and workflows.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "claude-cookbooks gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Claude Cookbooks is a collection of Jupyter notebooks demonstrating practical applications of Anthropic's Claude AI model, helping developers understand how to effectively leverage large language models for real-world tasks. The project stands out by providing hands-on, executable examples that reveal Claude's capabilities through concrete implementations rather than abstract descriptions. Developers can use these recipes as starting points for their own projects—from building conversational agents to automating document analysis—by modifying the provided code to experiment with different prompts and workflows.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/anthropics/claude-cookbooks for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
